; forces: 5
; Each force of Core is one thunk_force node in Mid (the roadmap's M10):
; the dump of Core to Mid holds five, one for each force here, and no
; more, for a value a let binds, a field read and a suspension passed on
; are none. The forces:
;   1, 2. sum's cases of its lazy x and y;
;   3. pick's case of its lazy b;
;   4. main's call of f, a suspension of pick t;
;   5. main's case of s, a suspension of f l r.
; p is bound to a constructor, a value, and its fields l and r go to f
; still suspended, l the CAF two, which sum forces as its x.
(data P () (P Int Int))

(val two Int (prim int_add 1 1))

(val sum (-> Int Int Int)
  (\ ((x Int) (y Int)) (case x a (_ (case y b (_ (prim int_add a b)))))))

(val pick (-> Bool (-> Int Int Int))
  (\ ((b Bool)) (case b c ((True) sum) ((False) sum))))

(val main (-> World (utuple World Int))
  (\ ((w World))
    (let (t Bool (con True))
    (let (f (-> Int Int Int) (pick t))
    (let (p P (con P two 3))
    (case p q
      ((P l r)
        (let (s Int (f l r))
          (case s v (_ (utuple w v)))))))))))
